    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d888">

                <pb facs="1032" n="952" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg952"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Sickles.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March 21,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 427.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                    Storer’s No. 642, of the 3d instant, reporting the position assumed by the
                    Spanish authorities in the case of Antonio Gisbert y Bayot.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that the Department is of opinion that it is perhaps not
                    unreasonable for those authorities to require Mr. Gisbert to show the place of
                    his residence on April 11, 1899, the date of the exchange of ratifications of
                    the treaty of peace.</p>
                <p>As his mother has gone to Manila to obtain the necessary evidence, no further
                    action seems to be required at this time.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
